*> Item frames (docs/protocol/34-entity-models-9-non-living-entities.md section 10; display context fixed of 12 section 8.2): the replica keeps a frame's direction (entry 8, DIRECTION), item
*> (entry 9) and rotation (entry 10), and draws the framed item: at the entity position, translate the direction's step x 0.46875, rotate X by 0 (vertical: -90 x the step, rotate Y 180) then Y
*> by 180 - toYRot, translate z 0.4375 (0.5 when invisible: flags bit 32), rotate Z by rotation x 45 degrees, scale 0.5, then the item's fixed display transform (item/generated: rotation (0, 180, 0)).
*> Expected vertices of the stick's two quads from an independent script (scratchpad/models/frame_items.py, written from the document text). A glow frame is full bright, a stone is a cube (36
*> vertices), an empty frame draws nothing.
